the third episode of the book of boba  fett really pushed two ideas that boba  fett is supposed to be absolutely  terrifying and that he's basically the  godfather welcome back to streaming the  galaxy i'm rocket riley and the book of  boba fett episode 3 the streets of  mosespa was just released on disney plus  and it was jam-packed full of action and  intense storytelling now let's dive into  a complete breakdown and review of the  episode looking at all the easter eggs  and references you may have missed as  well as the parallels between boba fett  and the godfather don vito corleone the  episode starts us off with a bit of  exposition where the ex-torture droid  explains that most espo was split into  three crime factions after the sail  barge disaster calling back to the  events of return of the jedi where boba  fett ended up in the sarlacc pit the  three crime factions seem quite similar  to the rivaling crime families that you  may see in mobster movies such as the  godfather or goodfellas this  presentation is interrupted however by a  visit from a water merchant upset about  some street youths who keep stealing his  water this interaction is very similar  to scenes in mobster movies where people  come to request things from the dawn  mostly in the form of protection so boba  fett goes into the streets of mo cesar  and finds the ing who had been stealing  from the water merchant and he finds  they're only stealing because there's no  work to be found the gang is made up of  humans who have body enhancements from  droids very similar to something you may  see in cyberpunk 2077 or elita battle  angel boba then hires them to join his  crime family and goes back to the palace  in his back to tank boba has yet another  flashback to his time with the tuscan  raiders and he travels to mosul to meet  with the pike syndicate which we saw in  the first couple episodes of the series  as well as in the animated star wars  series he passes by someone placing  stormtrooper helmets on spikes a scene  we first saw in the mandalorian we also  see a woman with three pet droids who is  most certainly pele motto the mechanic  who we also first met in the mandalorian  these two references undoubtedly point  to the idea that the book of boba fett  is basically a season two and a half for  the mandalorian after meeting with the  pikes who tell him they can't pay  tribute because they already paid it to  the swoop gang bubba returns to his home  with the tuscans but finds it destroyed  with every member of his new family dead  this calls back to the scene where luke  returned to his home to find his aunt  and uncle dead and everything destroyed  as well the scenes that follow are  highly emotional since we've come to a  greater appreciation for the tuscans and  their culture as the mandalorian and the  book of boba fett have portrayed these  individuals in a completely different  light similar to how the building of the  gaffy stick mirrors jedi building their  lightsabers the funeral pyre the tuscans  were placed on in their deaths mirrors  the funeral pyres jedi were placed upon  at their deaths this just points to the  idea that there are likely even more  similarities between tuscan culture and  jedi mysticism boba is then ripped out  of his flashback as black crysanton  pulls him out of his back to tank and  throws him across the room this fight  scene is one of the coolest we've seen  so far since we finally get to see  exactly what a wookie is capable of in  combat the only time we've seen  something close to this is in the final  scenes on kessel and solo a star wars  story when chewie helped the prisoners  escape we also get to see some of the  new crime family members bodily  enhancements with one even using an  electric whip although they aren't able  to overpower chrysanthemum they do trap  him in the pit below the throne room  later the hutt twins arrive to apologize  with a gift for boba fett a rancor which  is lying beside danny trejo who is now  officially a part of the star wars  universe this rancor could be moochie  the young rancor we met in the bad batch  the huts then explained that they're  leaving tatooine and that boba should  too since most vespa has been promised  to another crime cindy kit likely  meaning the pikes although they could  mean crimson dawn which is currently  being led by kira who we saw in solo a  star wars story the twins explained that  war is bad for business which job of the  hutt frequently said before his death  and then they leave tatooine danny  trejo's character later explains to boba  the lighter side of rancors saying the  witches of dathomir used to ride them  these witches were seen in the clone  wars television series as well as in the  video game jedi fallen order it's  explained that rancors are quite calm  and less provoked and that they imprint  upon the first person they see since  boba says that he wants to learn how to  write it similar to how he wrote a giant  creature in the star wars holiday  special in which he first appeared boba  is the first person the rancor sees  starting their bond which will surely  grow over time boba and phoenix shand  head to the mayor's palace which leads  to a speeder chase this chase scene is  very reminiscent of scenes from american  graffiti which showcased similarly  bright-colored car scenes and which was  also directed by george lucas at one  point one of the speeders actually  crashes through an oil painting of jabba  which is a bit silly and the scene ends  with the mayor's major domo crashing  sideways into a cart full of fruit  calling back to when biff crashed into a  truck full of fertilizer in back to the  future the major domo then confesses  that the mayor is working with the pike  syndicate the pikes arrive on tatooine  fenix says that they're going to war and  boba says that they will be ready it'll  be very interesting to see how this war  plays out since it'll likely be very  similar to crime family wars we've seen  in mobster movies the outcome of this  war will likely depend heavily upon who  the city's leaders and rich elites  support whether it be boba fett or the  pykes overall this episode was great  although there were a few scenes which  seemed a bit unnecessary the scene where  boba bonded with the rancor and the  black crystal fight scene were  phenomenal i really can't wait to see  where the series takes us and if you're  interested to see where the upcoming  obi-wan kenobi series will take us check  out this video also don't forget to  subscribe like this video and thanks for  watching  [Music]  you
 

